      "units": [
        {
          "id": "s3-intro-01",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Need to keep a customer upload or a backup and retrieve it later? Amazon S three stores those files as objects without making you provision disks.",
          "text_sha256": "60d7993947d2ca7cd0ff9fba409eeea7d1244952fc4c52f9934833bac2802808",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a7a9f1818c767620784686034fef9b03dd9ff2fe34c38826b306572163e46ce8",
          "asset_sha256": "a329ce0360f8726528d965ce480ca5b9258c3bc01ab6a526d4810df2eab4701c"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-intro-02",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Think of an object as the file plus metadata, like its content type. The bucket is the container, and the key is the object's full name inside it.",
          "text_sha256": "3aec0380046b09d4dc567547ee2b48150f00f8fcb6e8739b7c43f07cf0512ce1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3aec0380046b09d4dc567547ee2b48150f00f8fcb6e8739b7c43f07cf0512ce1",
          "asset_sha256": "3253b90c0d7384fcaae1d1c3af9694db66f4f126feba58ce4ebd2161bb98f2e5"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-intro-03",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Here the bucket is course uploads, and the key is images slash logo dot P N G. That slash is part of the name, not a folder you need to create.",
          "text_sha256": "aaaf3eb4776f338086d54a7f0e0bf42e08295117329113a445ad4e04f9cb35fa",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "aaaf3eb4776f338086d54a7f0e0bf42e08295117329113a445ad4e04f9cb35fa",
          "asset_sha256": "3253b90c0d7384fcaae1d1c3af9694db66f4f126feba58ce4ebd2161bb98f2e5"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-intro-04",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "S three Standard is designed for eleven nines of durability and ninety-nine point nine nine percent availability. Durability is about keeping the data. Availability is about being able to reach it when you need it.",
          "text_sha256": "81446d91a2a39f1d3e919f31b354439e75c5e955a66340adb83cd649d094ab75",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "eaeee6cc25e8840b3ea0bab300e882d5bbd213680db664a88010767cfe93a7bf",
          "asset_sha256": "06324d52264568052d86da026de4c07da90401aa51a29211985f1f80799ca4d8"
        },
        {
          "id": "s3-intro-05",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Choose a storage class based on how often you need access and what it costs. If versioning is enabled, you can recover a previous version.",
          "text_sha256": "09ab162790e0f155187e311b01d1dee55817a481e966cc80be9c8f60036f61b1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "09ab162790e0f155187e311b01d1dee55817a481e966cc80be9c8f60036f61b1",
          "asset_sha256": "06324d52264568052d86da026de4c07da90401aa51a29211985f1f80799ca4d8"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
